southwest medical the sponsor of this  next segment is home to many of our  local hospice care heroes rocky spoke to  a doctor about the hospice services they  provide and addresses the questions  people frequently ask  you always have such great information  about hospice care i'm with southwest  medical we're kind of debunking the  myths and also telling the truth about  it so let's just start with you know  what is hospice care let's define it for  people  so hospice care is a level of care  that's really appropriate when patients  have a  life-limiting illness where they there  are no more curative options  and the patient and their family choose  to  embrace the time that they have and  instead of spending that time pursuing a  cure and visiting doctors  they do whatever they want to do and we  support them in that and we bring the  care to their home  on their schedule the question is now  let's get into these frequently asked  questions  is hospice a place that people must go  so hospice is absolutely not a place  hospice is a level of care and service  that people have to be eligible for  and something like 98 of our patients  are cared for in their home or wherever  they were living before hospice started  so if they're in a group home or in  assisted living or  in an apartment wherever they live  there are different levels of care  within hospice so sometimes a patient  may have unmanaged symptoms that qualify  them to go  to an inpatient unit for short-term care  so hospice is never supposed to provide  the place to live and we never make  patients leave their home is hospice  care expensive  so hospice care  is covered by medicare and medicaid and  just about every commercial insurance  so  for most patients there's not medicare  and medicaid there's no copay most  commercial insurances there's no co-pay  hospice is basically free to the patient  and medicare and medicaid pay the  hospice for the care that's provided how  long can someone be in hospice care  so the the criteria for hospice care are  on paper if you will at medicare it says  that an individual will have a prognosis  of six months or fewer so they're not  expected to long to live longer than six  months  we have had patients in hospice care for  four years  hospice  does not put an expiration date on the  patient or the service  we just recertify the patient and we go  out and make sure they're still eligible  for the care  beautiful service and is hospice just  medication is a frequently asked  question  so hospice is not just medication so  hospices are responsible for for  providing all of  the medications  even a little bit related to the  patient's what we call terminal  diagnosis and also all of their  medications that are for comfort so an  antidepressant or pain medicine or  nausea medicine but we also provide and  i would say this is more important than  the medicine we provide the nurses and  the doctors and the social workers and  the chaplains  and a bereavement service so we provide  people  to help the patient and their family  understand what's happening and not be  afraid of it  we want to thank southwest medical for  sponsoring this segment they serve all  across southern nevada and if you want  more information you can call that  number 702-877-5199  or visit their website at smalv.com  we'll be right back
 

